---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";
import Card from "../components/Card.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import Pill from "../components/Pill.astro";
import { siteStats } from "../lib/site";
import { WEBMCP_SURFACES, WEBMCP_TOOL_COUNT } from "../lib/webmcp/catalog";

/*
 * The agents page. Two rails, told in order: the MCP server a coding agent
 * connects to from an editor, then WebMCP, where the agent driving a browser
 * works this site next to the person.
 *
 * This is the detail context, so it is allowed to go technical - the flag
 * path and the tool names live here and nowhere else. The marketing sections
 * that link to it stay in plain words.
 */

const stats = await siteStats();
---

<Layout
  title="Icons for AI agents - MCP server and WebMCP | Motificons"
  description={`Give Claude Code, Codex and Cursor ${stats.icons} icons over MCP - and let the AI agent in your browser search, restyle and collect them on the site itself.`}
>
  <Header active="agents" />

  <main id="main" class="pb-24">
    <div class="page-container">
      <h1 class="pt-14 text-h2 font-bold sm:text-hero">
        Stop letting your agent guess icons.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-ink-muted">
        Agents get the same library you get: {stats.icons}+ open-source icons,
        your collections, your style. There are two ways in. Your coding agent
        connects to the Motificons server from your editor, over MCP. Or the AI
        agent in your browser works this site with you, over WebMCP - searching
        the grid, restyling the preview and filling your collection while you
        watch.
      </p>

      {/* Status strip: both rails shipped - MCP 2026-08-10, WebMCP 2026-08-31. */}
      <div class="mt-8 rounded-card bg-banner px-6 py-4 text-ink">
        <p>
          <strong class="font-bold">Both are live.</strong>
          {" "}The MCP server is free with an account: make a key in the
          dashboard and connect your agent in a minute. The browser tools need
          no setup at all - they are already on every page, and a browser agent
          that supports WebMCP finds them the moment it asks what the page can
          do.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">In your editor: the MCP server</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
          Claude Code, Codex and Cursor point at the Motificons server and get
          the library, your collections and production-ready code without
          leaving the editor.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
          <Card variant="blue">
            <Icon name="search" size={24} class="text-ink" />
            <h3 class="mt-4 text-h3 font-semibold">Search by intent</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-meta">
              Your agent asks for "something for archived items" and gets
              candidates that actually read that way, not fifty near-duplicates
              of a box.
            </p>
          </Card>

          <Card variant="teal">
            <Icon name="grid" size={24} class="text-ink" />
            <h3 class="mt-4 text-h3 font-semibold">
              Your collections are the source of truth
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-meta">
              You curate collections visually here; the agent consumes them
              there, and can add what it picks back into the collection. Curated
              by a human, consumed by a machine.
            </p>
          </Card>

          <Card variant="grape">
            <Icon name="check" size={24} class="text-ink" />
            <h3 class="mt-4 text-h3 font-semibold">Audit your repo</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-meta">
              Point it at your codebase and it reports mixed sets, orphan SVGs
              and off-collection icons - checked against your curated system,
              not generic heuristics.
            </p>
          </Card>
        </div>

        <h3 class="mt-10 text-h3 font-semibold">Setup</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
          A few lines in your agent's MCP config, using the API key that comes
          with your free account. Create it from your dashboard's "Coding agents (MCP)"
          section, which also has ready-made, copy-paste configs for Claude
          Code, Cursor and Codex with your key already filled in.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">In your browser: WebMCP</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
          WebMCP is a new browser standard. Instead of leaving an AI agent to
          guess at the buttons on a page, the page tells it what it can do.
          Motificons offers {WEBMCP_TOOL_COUNT} things an agent can do here, and
          every one of them is something you can do yourself: it presses the
          site's real controls, on the page you have open, while you watch.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
          <Card variant="violet">
            <Icon name="search" size={24} class="text-ink" />
            <h3 class="mt-4 text-h3 font-semibold">It works the real site</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-meta">
              The search runs in the grid you are looking at. The filter pills
              flip. The preview restyles. The tile lands in your collection.
              Nothing happens in a tab you cannot see.
            </p>
          </Card>

          <Card variant="blue">
            <Icon name="check" size={24} class="text-ink" />
            <h3 class="mt-4 text-h3 font-semibold">It can only do what you can</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-meta">
              The agent acts as you, in your session, through the same routes
              your own clicks take. Same limits, same rules. There is no back
              door and nothing it can reach that you cannot.
            </p>
          </Card>

          <Card variant="teal">
            <Icon name="star" size={24} class="text-ink" />
            <h3 class="mt-4 text-h3 font-semibold">You can take over</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-meta">
              Scroll, click, edit, undo, close the tab - the page is still
              yours. When the pick is a taste call, the agent can open the Add
              icons panel and hand it back to you instead of choosing.
            </p>
          </Card>
        </div>

        <h3 class="mt-10 text-h3 font-semibold">
          What the agent can do, page by page
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
          Tools appear and disappear with the page: an agent on the icon
          library gets the search tools, an agent on one of your collections
          gets the collection tools. Nothing is offered where it would not work.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto scroll-light">
          <table class="w-full min-w-[720px] border-collapse text-left">
            <caption class="sr-only">
              WebMCP tools this site offers, by page
            </caption>
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b-2 border-ink">
                <th scope="col" class="py-4 pr-4 text-body font-bold">Page</th>
                <th scope="col" class="py-4 pr-4 text-body font-bold">Tool</th>
                <th scope="col" class="py-4 text-body font-bold">What it does</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {
                WEBMCP_SURFACES.flatMap((surface) =>
                  surface.tools.map((tool, index) => (
                    <tr class="border-b border-ink/10 align-top">
                      {index === 0 && (
                        <th
                          scope="rowgroup"
                          rowspan={surface.tools.length}
                          class="py-4 pr-4 text-left font-normal"
                        >
                          <span class="font-semibold">{surface.surface}</span>
                          <span class="mt-1 block text-meta text-ink-muted">
                            {surface.where}
                          </span>
                        </th>
                      )}
                      <td class="py-4 pr-4 font-mono text-meta">{tool.name}</td>
                      <td class="py-4 text-meta">{tool.does}</td>
                    </tr>
                  )),
                )
              }
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">Try it</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
          Browser agents are new, so not many browsers can do this yet. Two
          work today.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
          <Card variant="blue">
            <Icon name="bolt" size={24} class="text-ink" />
            <h3 class="mt-4 text-h3 font-semibold">In Chrome</h3>
            <ol class="mt-3 flex list-decimal flex-col gap-2 pl-5 text-meta">
              <li>
                Chrome 149 or newer. Open
                {" "}<span
                  class="rounded-tag bg-surface px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-meta"
                  >chrome://flags/#enable-webmcp-testing</span
                >
                {" "}and switch it on.
              </li>
              <li>Restart the browser when it asks.</li>
              <li>
                Open motificons.app and ask the browser's AI for the icons you
                need.
              </li>
            </ol>
          </Card>

          <Card variant="teal">
            <Icon name="sparkle" size={24} class="text-ink" />
            <h3 class="mt-4 text-h3 font-semibold">
              In the ChatGPT desktop app
            </h3>
            <ol class="mt-3 flex list-decimal flex-col gap-2 pl-5 text-meta">
              <li>Open its built-in browser. Nothing to switch on.</li>
              <li>Go to motificons.app.</li>
              <li>
                Ask for the job, not the clicks: "find four outline icons for a
                settings screen and put them in a collection".
              </li>
            </ol>
          </Card>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-6 text-meta text-ink-muted">
          Anywhere else, nothing changes: the tools are simply never asked for,
          and the site works exactly as it does for everybody.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-h2 font-semibold">Get started</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <Button href="/dashboard">Connect your agent</Button>
          <Button variant="secondary" href="/register">Create a free account</Button>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <Pill variant="yellow">Free with an account</Pill>
          <Pill variant="teal">No usage limit</Pill>
          <Pill variant="gray">No card needed</Pill>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
